{
  "about": "The work-folder op rule (docs/dev/work_folders.md \"The op rule\"): who may change a work folder's file and its folders. trees: folder trees by name, [{id, parent (null at the top), vault?: the mark {pull, library}}]. Each case names its tree and its writer: person (a tab, a share editor, the AI, an import), vault (op client disk) or mirror (op client sync). allowed says whether the rule lets it through; kind, on a refusal, names the words a person reads (filing.refusal_text: filed, named, trash, restore, directories, remove, document). patch: filing.root_patch(tree, before, patch, content, writer, target_is_file) on a page root, result the patch as stored when it differs from patch. create: filing.creation(tree, props, writer, target_is_file), result the props as stored when they differ. trash: filing.may_trash(tree, props, writer). restore: filing.may_restore(tree, props, writer), result the props when they differ (a stale stamp dropped). tree: filing.tree_op(tree, op, writer) on the folders pseudo-page, op {op, id, parent?, content?, props?}. A patch's null removes its key. Read by backend/tests/test_work_folders_filing.py and frontend/tests/workFolders.test.mjs (frontend/src/explorer/workFolders.js).",
